description:
The kernel and user mode name the same things differently. A driver creates `\Device\XenonEcho`, links it as `\??\XenonEcho`, and its client opens `\\.\XenonEcho`; `C:\Notes` is `\??\C:\Notes` to the kernel; the driver's registry path is `\REGISTRY\MACHINE\...` while regedit shows `HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\...`. Write the conversions a driver and its tools need (milestone 2 uses them):

```cpp
bool validBaseName(const std::string& base);
std::string deviceName(const std::string& base);       // "\Device\<base>"
std::string linkName(const std::string& base);         // "\??\<base>"
std::string userPath(const std::string& base);         // "\\.\<base>"
std::string win32ToNt(const std::string& path);
std::string ntToWin32(const std::string& nt);
std::string serviceName(const std::string& registryPath);
std::string userRegistryPath(const std::string& registryPath);
```

- **validBaseName**: 1 to 32 characters, letters and digits only, starting with a letter. The three name functions return `""` for an invalid base.
- **win32ToNt**: `C:\x` (a drive letter, colon and backslash) → `\??\C:\x`; `\\server\share\x` → `\??\UNC\server\share\x`; `\\.\Name` → `\??\Name`; `\\?\C:\x` → `\??\C:\x`; `\\?\UNC\server\x` → `\??\UNC\server\x`. Anything else (relative paths, `C:x`, `\x`) cannot be converted without a current directory: return `""`.
- **ntToWin32** reverses it: `\??\UNC\...` → `\\...`; `\??\C:\...` (a drive) → `C:\...`; `\??\Name` (anything else after `\??\`) → `\\.\Name`; `\DosDevices\` is the same as `\??\` (in any letter case); `\Device\...` → `\\?\GLOBALROOT\Device\...`; anything else → `""`.
- **serviceName**: for a path starting with `\REGISTRY\MACHINE\SYSTEM\` then `CurrentControlSet` or `ControlSet` followed by three digits, then `\Services\<name>` (and nothing after the name), return the name; else `""`. Comparisons ignore case; the name keeps its case.
- **userRegistryPath**: `\REGISTRY\MACHINE\rest` → `HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\rest`, `\REGISTRY\USER\rest` → `HKEY_USERS\rest` (prefix case ignored, `rest` unchanged); else `""`.

